# Local Transcriber

A **local Mac desktop app** for transcribing sales calls (and any audio/video)
entirely offline. Drag-and-drop or add files, pick a model per file and a
global language, and it converts, transcribes on-device with `mlx-whisper`
(Apple Silicon/Metal), and writes a clean `.md` transcript to `~/Downloads`.
No cloud, no OpenAI API, no external server. It tracks a local history and uses
it to predict how long the next transcription will take.

Multi-track sources (e.g. Zoom's per-participant recording) are detected via
`ffprobe` and transcribed track-by-track into pause-delimited, speaker-labeled
dialogue blocks (with real `(interrupting)` overlap detection). Single mixed
tracks stay plain text — no speaker guessing.

Stack: Python + `mlx-whisper` / `parakeet-mlx`, ffmpeg, a native Mac UI. Code
lives in `src/` (transcription, audio-track handling, dialogue blocking,
history DB, markdown writer) and `app/` (UI, worker, jobs).

## Layout
- `src/`, `app/`, `tests/`, `scripts/` — the app.
- `testing/` — a benchmark harness comparing transcription backends (timing +
  a rating UI). Shares the app's venv; the only backend needing a secret is
  Groq (`GROQ_API_KEY`, optional).
- `updates/` — AI Control update history.

## Secrets
- `GROQ_API_KEY` — **optional**, only for the Groq benchmark backends in
  `testing/`. The app itself needs no secrets (fully offline).

## Status
Adopted under AI Control on 2026-09-22. Flattened from a nested
`local-transcriber/` folder into the project root and its git history elevated
here. See `issues.txt` for open items.
